    "done_when": "tests/test_producer_reads_only_what_changed.py gains two cases. The first replaces a stream with a new file at least as long as the recorded offset (a new inode). The second rewrites a stream in place at the same inode with new content at least as long as the offset. Each shows the producer re-reading from zero and observing the new records. Both cases fail with the cursor check removed: the review of producer-reads-only-what-changed found that the current replacement case passes without the inode comparison, and that an in-place rewrite still resumes from the stale offset (reckon/_backends.py observe_log, reckon/crew/recovery.py _observed_stream). The commits-beyond-base cache in reckon/crew/recovery.py evicts entries for worktrees no longer live, and a case shows the cache staying bounded across many classified runs. The declared negative control is executed and logged. Base and head arms of tests/test_producer_reads_only_what_changed.py, tests/test_pointer_classification_is_memoised.py and tests/test_producer_shares_the_classifier_verdict.py show zero added failures.",
